From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:02:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: scan all eMMC HS200
 delay cells

At HS200 the station's eMMC reads correct data, but its multi-block
reads fail now and then without a log line, and the block driver
re-reads each such request one sector at a time.

mtk-sd scans an eMMC over 32 pad delay cells by default, setting CMD
and DATA to one shared value. The vendor kernel's HS200 tuning on this
eMMC (a 200 MHz clock, 49 cells to a cycle) finds the read data
failing at cells 14-20 and passing from 21 to 60. It sets DATA to
about 40 and CMD on its own. Run over the vendor's pass maps, a
32-cell scan's widest rising-edge window is 21-31, too short to skip
the falling edge, and its centre, 26, sits six cells above the failing
zone. A 64-cell scan finds 21-57 and picks 39, where the vendor lands.

MT6797 has the second delay fields at PAD_TUNE1 (0xf4) that mtk-sd
uses past 32 cells, and the microSD host already scans 64.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 0f691f5..1f242fd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -687,6 +687,12 @@
 	max-frequency = <200000000>;
 	cap-mmc-highspeed;
 	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
+
+	/*
+	 * Scan all 64 delay cells. The data window on this eMMC sits above the
+	 * first 32, and a 32-cell scan centres CMD and DATA near its lower edge.
+	 */
+	mediatek,tuning-step = <64>;
 };
 
